## Why This Is Asked
This question tests building lightweight, on-device NLP under strict memory and latency constraints, handling code-switching and multilingual input.

## Key Concepts
- On-device NLP, memory budgeting, latency targets
- Code-switching handling with language routing
- Lightweight lexical resources plus small ML fallback

## Code Example
```javascript
function correctWord(word, dict) {
  // simple one-edit distance correction
  if (dict.has(word)) return word;
  // naive neighbor search: insert/delete/replace
  // (illustrative; real impl would be optimized)
  for (const w of dict) {
    if (levDistance(word, w) <= 1) return w;
  }
  return word;
}
```

